"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a focus on leveraging AI for data visualization and secure file sharing. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing ahead of schedule. The project budget was adjusted to $550,000 to cover scope requirements, including real-time analytics, and a $15,000 training budget was approved for the coding team and project managers. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, were updated for implementation in January. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was requested by the end of November. A celebration for reaching the testing milestone was held on October 10th."
